/-!
# Higher direct images and colimits of abelian sheaves

Let `f : (C, J) ⟶ (D, K)` be a morphism of sites, given by a continuous functor
`u : D ⥤ C`, let `(F_i)` be a system of abelian sheaves on `C` and let `p ≥ 0`. Write `B` for
the set of objects `V` of `D` over which degree-`p` cohomology commutes with the colimit, that
is for which `H^p(u(V), colim F_i) = colim H^p(u(V), F_i)`. Stacks 0H7B says that if every
object of `D` has a covering by elements of `B`, then
`R^p f_* (colim F_i) = colim R^p f_* F_i`.

By Stacks 072W, `R^p f_*` is the sheafification of the presheaf `V ↦ H^p(u(V), -)`, i.e. of
the right derived functor of `sheafToPresheaf ⋙ (restriction along uᵒᵖ)`; and sheafification,
being a left adjoint, commutes with colimits. So the whole content is that the *presheaf*
`V ↦ H^p(u(V), -)` sheafifies to the colimit, which needs only that its sections commute with
the colimit over a covering family of every object — and that is the hypothesis.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Cohomology.HigherDirectImage.preservesColimit_rightDerived_sheafPushforwardContinuous`
  (Stacks 0H7B): the local criterion in `PreservesColimit` form.
* `Stacks.Cohomology.HigherDirectImage.isIso_colimit_post_rightDerived_sheafPushforwardContinuous`:
  the same criterion stated for the canonical comparison morphism, when colimits of the given
  shape exist in the coefficient category.

## Implementation notes

The source writes its two canonical identifications as equalities of objects. They are
rendered here as `CategoryTheory.Limits.PreservesColimit`, which asserts exactly that the
canonical comparison is an isomorphism and is natural; stating it this way means no colimit of
an unrelated diagram has to exist in the coefficient category, and a supplied colimit of the
original diagram then produces the colimits of the local cohomology diagrams and of the
higher-direct-image diagram. The `IsIso (colimit.post …)` form is derived from it for the case
where the colimits do exist.

Only *continuity* of `u` is used, not that it comes from a morphism of sites, so the statement
is made under that weaker hypothesis. The two site universes, the coefficient universe and the
diagram universe are independent.

"Every object has a covering by elements of `B`" is spelled with a `PreZeroHypercover` whose
generating sieve is a covering sieve, which is what the proof consumes; internally it is
converted to `GrothendieckTopology.HasEnoughObjects`, the predicate that quantifies over the
generating family rather than over all covering sieves.

Additivity of the sections functors and of the direct image, which is what makes
`Functor.rightDerived` applicable, comes from the general instances
`CategoryTheory.Sheaf.additive_sheafSections_obj` and
`CategoryTheory.Functor.additive_sheafPushforwardContinuous`; both are stated for an arbitrary
preadditive coefficient category.

The private helpers are generic: `presheafCoconeDesc_existsUnique` is the universal property of
an objectwise colimit of presheaves against a *sheaf*, proved by amalgamating the local descents
over the sieve generated by the good objects, and `presheafToSheaf_mapCocone_isColimit` is the
consequence that sheafification carries such a cocone to a colimit cocone — Stacks 0038 and
00W1 in the form this lemma uses them. Each has a primed form for a site whose category need
not be small.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0H7B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0H7B)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 072W](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/072W)
-/

@[expose] public section

